From 6eb2d971866a1bdc9646bd708f28b5fb4473b9af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:09:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Tools_OtherSettings: surface the three shell-only Reaper
 knobs

A survey of Reaper's nvram found exactly three settings with no GUI path at all -
everything else in the reaper_/rwarden_/rmcp_ namespaces is reachable, mostly
through reaper_dev.cgi or reaper_fw.cgi with the key passed as a PARAMETER, which
is why a name-search of the .asp files under-reports it badly. All three now have
controls in a Reaper section on the stock Tweaks page.

  reaper_inject   theme kill switch. No defaults.c entry on purpose: the code
                  reads unset/nonzero as ON and only a literal "0" as off, so
                  initial() must map empty to ON or the page would show a
                  freshly flashed router as themeless. action_script gains
                  restart_httpd, since that is when it takes effect.

  wlcsm_bindfix   the WLCSM netlink bind() shim. DEFAULT FLIPPED 0 -> 1 per
                  owner instruction. Needs a reboot, and the page says so.

  rwarden_sched   Warden feed-refresh cron. The only rwarden_* setting that was
                  never surfaced.

Stock page, so it uses the stock idiom - .FormTable rows, plain selects, the
page's existing submit path - rather than Reaper-native styling, which
reaper_content.css would fight.

rwarden_sched is charset-validated client-side to exactly what rw_valid_sched()
accepts in rc/rwarden.c (digits, space, * / , -). That consumer already rejects
anything else and falls back to 30 4 * * *, so the field cannot become an
injection path even though the value reaches cru unquoted; the client check
exists so the user is told rather than silently getting the default.

The defaults.c comment was rewritten alongside the value. It previously explained
at length why the shim was off, and leaving that next to "1" would have left the
code contradicting itself - the same trap already recorded against the Wireless
auto-scan item, where one of two disagreeing comments has to change.

RTWK_00-RTWK_07 minted, English-seeded in all 25 packs, lockstep 6627 -> 6635.

Checked: no sysdep/FUNCTION variant shadows this page, so the base file is the
one that ships (rule 33). defaults.prep is untracked and gitignored - an artifact
generated from defaults.c for calc_nvram, not a second source of truth. The one
non-ASCII byte in the page is a pre-existing UTF-8 BOM, unchanged. Build gate
clean, and all seven inline script blocks still parse in all 25 languages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
